# Shell scripts must keep LF endings.
#
# A Windows checkout previously shipped CRLF, non-executable scripts to the VPS.
# Cron invokes three of them directly, so every job — backup, healthcheck and
# notification processing — died silently into a log file for ten days
# ("/bin/sh: ...: Permission denied", 10,072 failures in the health log).
# The VPS gets these files as a plain copy of this working tree (there is no
# git checkout there), and `core.autocrlf` keeps CRLF in the working tree — so
# without eol=lf here, everything below ships to Linux with CRLF endings. That is
# the defect that broke every cron script on 2026-09-06.
*.sh text eol=lf
*.bash text eol=lf
deploy/*.conf text eol=lf
deploy/*.yml text eol=lf
deploy/*.sql text eol=lf
